A||N||5||alpha1||What is wrong with my Fiero?||||1||
Z||000000||alpha1||11-27-2001||05:32 PM||||I can't figure out for the life of my what is wrong with my 86 GT, auto... Here is what happens...<P>I start it up... drive for usually about a minute... the engine stumbles (usually on acceleration) and the check engine light comes on. It then continues to run open loop (and fairly crappy) until I shut down and let the car be for a while.<P>I ran the ECM codes and get three... EGR, lean exhaust, and ignition failure (Code 44 I think).<P>I disabled the EGR and it does the same thing. I checked all the wiring and everything is at least connected and intact.<P>Any ideas with regards to what my problem might be?<P>Thanks in advance,<P>--Doug Knight||||reg||1
Z||000001||Matthew_Fiero||11-27-2001||06:25 PM||||I also have that engine code<BR>i haven'tg found the problem yet<BR>i assume it is the o2 sensor<BR>but that is yet to be confirmed||||reg||1
Z||000002||Eriamjh||11-27-2001||08:16 PM||||Heh.  A lean fuel code means too much air or too little fuel.<P>Where does fuel come from?  The tank!  Where does is go through?  The fuel filter!  change it.  Mine would not go over 60 mph and would only accelerate gradually because the filter was partially clogged.  It would pass only so much fuel at a time.<P>Also change the O2 sensor.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Old Lar||11-27-2001||08:31 PM||||Code 32 EGR system  Replace EGR valve, vacuum leak, EGR solinoid.<P>Code 44 Lean exhaust  ECM wiring connection, terminals 15 and 8. Vacuum leak at TBI base gasket,vacuum hoses or intake manifold gasket. Replace oxygen sensor.<P>The Haynes manual has no error code for ignition failure.  Relace distributor cap, pickup coil, ignition modual or distributor.<P>You may have a crudded up TB.  Check for carbon build up in the TB.<P>Could be a clogged fuel filter and the injectors aren't getting enough gas.  Bad spark plugs, wires, incorrect timing.<P>Too many potential problems.  Find a Fiero friendly mechanic.||||reg||1
Z||000004||CraigC||11-27-2001||08:38 PM||||I looked into my GM service manual and a code 44 is definitely a lean exhaust indication. Some part of the problem can be:<BR>Fuel pressure - should be 62-90 kPA (9-13PSI)<BR>Do you have water in the fuel?<BR>Is the EGR good?<BR>How about MAP sensor<BR>If all the above are ok it's probably the oxygen sensor.But I would also try the Fuel filter.<BR>If all else fails try the ECM.<BR>||||reg||3
Z||000005||GTDude||11-27-2001||10:01 PM||||It's prob the egr solenoid or the egr valve sticking open....take it off and clean it with carb cleaner...make sure the pinacle is seating.  As for the code 42 (it should be) if it has to do with the module and timing, it's prob. the computer itself.....they are known for cracked circuit boards.||||reg||1
